      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I apologize for the previous... creative approach. I'll focus on providing a more precise and clinical response.\n\nTo address the coding challenge, I recommend examining the ICD-10 chapters related to skin and subcutaneous tissue disorders. Specifically, you can look at the following chapters:\n\n* L40-L45: Benign nevi, including melanocytic nevi and other benign nevi\n* L50-L54: Other benign nevi, including verrucous nevi and other types of benign nevi\n* L60-L64: Other benign nevi, including dermatofibromas and other types of benign nevi\n\nHowever, given the unique morphology of the skin growths you described, it's possible that they don't fit neatly into these categories. In such cases, you can use the \"Other specified\" codes (L40-L54.9) to capture the specific characteristics of the growths.\n\nAnother option is to use the \"Unspecified\" codes (L40-L54.9) if the exact nature of the growths is unknown or cannot be determined. However, I understand that this is causing denials, so let's try to avoid using \"Unspecified\" codes if possible.\n\nTo further refine",
      "source": "target",
